      "response": "\"The Arab Tent\" is an oil\u2011on\u2011canvas painting by the English Victorian artist Edwin (Henry)\u202fLandseer, dated around\u202f1865\u201366. It depicts an Arab mare with her foal, flanked by two Persian greyhounds and two monkeys\u2014one sporting an earring. Above, a jar with two pipes hints at the owner\u2019s presence. The work was shown at the Royal Academy in 1866 under the title \u201cMare and Foal \u2013 Indian Tent\u2026\u201d, though the tent is clearly Arab. \n\nThe Prince of Wales purchased it from Landseer in 1867, and Sir\u202fRichard Wallace acquired it in 1878, placing it in the Wallace Collection\u2019s Hall, where you\u2019ll find it now. Conservation work in 2017 was funded by Henrietta, Duchess of Bedford.",
